Upstream-Status: Inappropriate

Subject: [PATCH] mm/swap: Skip isolated CPUs in lru_add_drain_all() with isolcpus=lru

lru_add_drain_all() asks every online CPU whether it has something to
drain, reading its folio batches, its mlock batch and its buffer head
LRU.  With isolcpus=lru an isolated CPU never batches folios, and
bh_lru_install() already keeps buffer heads off isolated CPUs, so the
answer is always no -- but the question costs eight remote cachelines
per isolated CPU, homed on the isolated CPUs' node.  Under memory
pressure on the housekeeping CPUs those lines are no longer cached and
every call reads them from the isolated socket's DRAM.

Skip isolated CPUs in the loop when isolcpus=lru is set.
---
--- a/mm/swap.c
+++ b/mm/swap.c
@@ -882,6 +882,13 @@
 	for_each_online_cpu(cpu) {
 		struct work_struct *work = &per_cpu(lru_add_drain_work, cpu);
 
+		/*
+		 * With isolcpus=lru isolated CPUs never batch, and they never
+		 * cache buffer heads: don't read their batches from afar.
+		 */
+		if (cpu_is_isolated_strict(cpu, ISOL_STRICT_LRU))
+			continue;
+
 		if (cpu_needs_drain(cpu)) {
 			INIT_WORK(work, lru_add_drain_per_cpu);
 			queue_work_on(cpu, mm_percpu_wq, work);
